From fc37f3c14c779f34776fc2038dedd991d2443e0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:32:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 20/25] NativeLayerWayland: copy a stereo video's views in its
 own format

A stereo video whose views are not side by side with the left eye first
and visible across their whole width is copied into a buffer that holds
them so. The copy converted the video to 8-bit RGB: its colours were the
browser's conversion, not the compositor's; HDR video could not be
copied and stayed flat; and a surface that went from the video's own
buffers to RGB copies while playing (Swap Eyes, the user's choice, a
scroll that clips the video) switched buffer formats, which KWin 6.7 did
not survive.

A video with two planes (NV12, P010, P016) is now copied plane by plane
into a surface of its own format and colours
(DMABufSurfaceYUV::CreateCopyTarget), each view's visible part into its
half, the chroma at whole samples. Its colour representation stays on
the surface, the compositor converts it as it converts the video itself,
and HDR is kept. A few such surfaces are kept per layer, since the
compositor holds the one shown. Other formats, or a copy that fails,
still go to RGB, except HDR video, which then stays flat.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
